Chapter: DeskSheetPointTest
  cites Works chapter GopDesk
  cites Works chapter GopPrograms
  cites Works chapter GopFont
  cites UI chapter Widget
  cites UI chapter Layout
  cites Foreword chapter CCE

 WHERE TO CLICK, LAID FACELESS, WHICH IS NOT WHERE THE DESK PUTS IT.
 This lays the chrome and the start menu at the capture geometry and
 prints widget centres in DEVICE pixels. It lays them with `gfont-none`,
 so every width here comes from the eight-pixels-a-character fallback,
 while a desk that finds a TTF face on its medium lays a NARROWER band.
 Measured 2026-09-08 at 1600x900: this arm answers `menu` centre 156,848,
 and the button on the glass occupies x 34..147, y 830..847, centre
 90,838. A timeline written from this number clicks outside the widget
 and reads exactly like a bed that delivers no clicks. It cost six
 captures.

 SO THESE ARE NOT CLICK COORDINATES until this arm loads the face the
 desk loads. Take the pill and the menu rows from the PIXELS of a
 capture; use these numbers only to say whether an id RESOLVES, which is
 what the zero-width check is for.

 The numbers are printed and asserted at once. A rect of zero width means
 `widget-find` did not find the id, which is the failure this would
 otherwise hand to a screenshot to discover.

Section: Body

  dsp-yn : Boolean -> Text
  dsp-yn (v) = if v then "yes" else "NO"

  dsp-box : WidgetNode, Text -> LayoutRect
  dsp-box (laid) (id) =
    when widget-find laid id
      is Just (n) -> n.wn-bounds
      is None -> layout-rect 0 0 0 0

  dsp-laid : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> WidgetNode
  dsp-laid (ds) (w) (h) (s) =
    widget-layout (desk-chrome-with (desk-menu-tree (peek-32 ds desk-prog-cell) gfont-none s ds) w ds) (dk-theme-ds ds) (layout-rect 0 0 (w / s) (h / s))

  dsp-at : WidgetNode, Text, Integer -> Text
  dsp-at (laid) (id) (s) =
    let r = dsp-box laid id
    in id & " centre " & integer-to-text ((r.lr-x + r.lr-w / 2) * s) & "," & integer-to-text ((r.lr-y + r.lr-h / 2) * s) & "  found " & dsp-yn (r.lr-w > 0)

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console, Device.Port] Nothing = act
    let w = 1600
    in let h = 900
    in let ds = alloc-zeroed dk-ds-bytes 64
    in let ps = alloc-zeroed 64 64
    in let pp = poke-32 ds desk-prog-cell ps
    in let e = gpr-ensure ps
    in let s = ui-wscale w
    in let laid = dsp-laid ds w h s
    in act
      print-line-uni ("laid with gfont-none, so these are NOT click coordinates")
      print-line-uni ("scale " & integer-to-text s)
      print-line-uni (dsp-at laid "menu" s)
      print-line-uni (dsp-at laid "gpr-Sheets" s)
      print-line-uni (dsp-at laid "gpr-Clock" s)
    end
  end
